# The generated output of the three targets is committed on purpose: reading it is the point of
# this project, so a reviewer should see what the engine produces without having to run it.
# `npm run verify` regenerates it and fails if what is committed drifts from what the engine emits.
#
# The `--no-idioms` trees are a comparison the verification builds, not an artifact anyone reads,
# and the interpreter caches are not ours.
out/*-plain/
out/**/__pycache__/
out/**/.ruff_cache/
node_modules
